<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    PAK'nSAVE Albany, STATIC location.

    139 Don McKinnon Drive, Albany, Auckland 0632
    -36.73013, 174.70716

    Parks the device exactly at the store and leaves it there.

    WHAT THIS TESTS

    NOT didEnterRegion. There is no boundary crossing, so that will not fire.
    Use PaknSaveAlbany-Approach.gpx for arrival.

    This one exercises the other path: didDetermineState returning .inside,
    which is how the app recovers when you are already standing in a store, e.g.
    the Live Activity was dismissed on a previous visit and you never left.

    That path runs from didStartMonitoringFor in AppDelegate. It used to be
    broken: requestState(for:) was called immediately after startMonitoring,
    before iOS had begun tracking, so it reliably answered .unknown.

    USE

    Xcode, Debug, Simulate Location, PaknSaveAlbany

    Then force quit and relaunch the app while still simulating this location.
    That is the scenario the recovery path exists for.
-->
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Frydge" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">

    <wpt lat="-36.73013" lon="174.70716">
        <name>PAK'nSAVE Albany</name>
    </wpt>

</gpx>
